                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 6.</note>
                <head>Mr. J. R. Jones to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 54.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Brussels,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 11, 1870</date>. (Received August 24,
                    1870.)</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Mr. Motley telegraphed me yesterday, as follows:</p>
                <p>Please inform Generals Sheridan and Forsythe that Count Bismarck informs Count
                    Bernstorff that they will be welcome at headquarters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. R. JONES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
